WEBVTT

00:10.960 --> 00:15.510
<i>The overwhelming dazzle that Yuki Ogata gave off</i>

00:15.590 --> 00:22.140
<i>enamored all who saw it,</i>
<i>and made her into something transcendent.</i>

00:26.690 --> 00:30.650
<i>She was a legendary dancer. A sublime figure...</i>

00:30.730 --> 00:37.410
<i>As I watched her from so nearby,</i>
<i>I danced for just a sliver of that light...</i>

00:37.490 --> 00:41.950
<i>To approach my mother...</i>
<i>To keep myself from disappearing...</i>

00:50.050 --> 00:53.970
<i>But, when that became impossible...</i>

00:54.050 --> 00:58.010
<i>When I lost ballet, the only</i>
<i>thing I thought mattered in my life...</i>

01:00.850 --> 01:02.890
<i>...Shoko was there for me.</i>

01:02.980 --> 01:09.360
<i>Her unbroken smile was the only light I had left...</i>

01:10.770 --> 01:13.110
<i>Then I saw light aboard the Fuego...</i>

01:13.190 --> 01:15.900
<i>My heart raced as I soared through the air.</i>

01:15.990 --> 01:19.910
<i>I thought I had found</i>
<i>a replacement for my injured legs.</i>

01:20.780 --> 01:24.290
<i>But I was wrong.</i>

01:24.370 --> 01:29.210
<i>Instead, my mistake hurt</i>
<i>complete strangers, my entire family,</i>

01:29.290 --> 01:33.000
<i>and even killed a dear friend...</i>

03:45.600 --> 03:50.180
We hit the GGP base tomorrow. Come with me.

03:50.810 --> 03:53.140
It'll probably be an intense RideBack battle

03:53.230 --> 03:55.440
the likes of which you've never seen before.

03:57.070 --> 03:59.110
Have you lost interest?

03:59.190 --> 04:03.280
Or do you prefer Okakura's plan to flee the country

04:03.360 --> 04:08.620
and live a life of false security and endless running?

04:10.120 --> 04:13.120
What do you truly want to do?

04:13.210 --> 04:18.380
Mourn? Escape? Or get revenge, perhaps?

04:18.460 --> 04:22.920
Just being with people who don't
care about others' lives makes me sick!

04:23.010 --> 04:26.470
Momentary sentimentality achieves nothing.

04:26.550 --> 04:32.060
They went after Suzuri
thinking she was me. I killed her.

04:32.140 --> 04:34.230
Then do as you wish.

04:34.310 --> 04:38.810
A RideBack is nothing but
scrap metal without a rider's will.

04:38.900 --> 04:44.650
As you would rather stand still
and let your gift rot, you are unfit to ride.

04:44.740 --> 04:46.030
Get out of my sight.

04:49.160 --> 04:52.680
Closed until things return to normal

04:52.750 --> 04:56.170
Oh, no... We can't even buy flowers?

04:58.880 --> 05:03.280
Closed for now

04:59.500 --> 05:02.880
Let's go. Suzuri will understand.

05:58.100 --> 06:00.980
Everyone's going away...

06:02.150 --> 06:05.820
Let's go back, before the rain gets worse.

06:11.780 --> 06:13.870
Nanpu Kataoka arrested

06:13.870 --> 06:19.350
National Police Agency Notice

06:19.370 --> 06:22.360
Wanted

06:39.230 --> 06:42.770
You're calling me directly?
What if we're being wiretapped?

06:42.860 --> 06:46.490
Don't worry about it. I have official approval.

06:46.570 --> 06:48.360
Were you able to check the documents I sent?

06:48.450 --> 06:49.360
Yes.

06:49.450 --> 06:53.370
Hesner did develop new military
RideBacks as a last-ditch recovery effort,

06:53.450 --> 06:56.490
but the sale fell through
before they could be delivered.

06:57.250 --> 07:01.330
To make up for it, the GGP leadership,
closely attached to Hesner,

07:01.420 --> 07:05.750
took the reins and had them sold
to Japan as profitable police RideBacks.

07:06.710 --> 07:08.630
The issue is the enormous amount of money

07:08.720 --> 07:11.130
that exchanged hands behind the scenes.

07:11.220 --> 07:16.720
But we need proof, not suspicion.
Isn't that your guys' specialty?

07:16.810 --> 07:19.890
It sounds like we already have proof.

07:19.980 --> 07:22.810
Now we need to know how things will be handled

07:22.900 --> 07:25.690
after the evidence comes forth.

07:39.410 --> 07:40.450
Hey.

07:42.540 --> 07:44.630
Can we really trust them?

07:47.960 --> 07:51.630
I'll hold them to their word.
Even if it costs us our lives.

08:05.110 --> 08:06.360
How is Ogata?

08:06.440 --> 08:08.270
She's calmed down.

08:08.360 --> 08:12.070
Or more like trying her hardest to act calm.

08:14.160 --> 08:20.910
She wanted flowers for Suzuri
when I asked if she wanted anything...

08:21.000 --> 08:23.910
Are you sure you won't come with us?

08:24.000 --> 08:29.090
This escape will work!
I know people overseas, too!

08:31.050 --> 08:34.010
You're the only one I can leave Ogata with.

08:35.430 --> 08:36.890
I'm sorry.

08:41.220 --> 08:42.310
So stupid...

08:49.070 --> 08:51.190
Why are you dressed like that?

08:51.280 --> 08:53.860
We told you it's not safe to go out--

08:58.660 --> 09:01.620
You'll catch a cold. Let's go back to your room.

09:05.000 --> 09:07.330
It's rather quiet outside.

09:07.420 --> 09:10.790
All roads into the city have been sealed off.

09:12.170 --> 09:15.720
But, thanks to that, we can move inside it freely.

09:15.800 --> 09:19.720
What if they strike first? We have no backup plans.

09:19.800 --> 09:21.510
They won't attack.

09:22.390 --> 09:26.390
Do you think Romanov would simply kill me normally?

09:26.480 --> 09:30.110
He's like a ball of complexes wrapped into a man.

09:30.190 --> 09:33.940
He wishes to kill me on a RideBack.

09:34.030 --> 09:38.410
He and I both want payback
for what happened in Arizona.

09:42.660 --> 09:47.620
The gong won't sound until he's sure he has me.

09:47.710 --> 09:50.670
We're the ones who will signal the start of the fight.

09:57.300 --> 10:00.340
--Good luck.
--You can count on us.

10:23.370 --> 10:25.950
I guess it's goodbye to this city for a while.

10:27.290 --> 10:30.250
I'll be joining you in the helicopter tomorrow.

10:31.500 --> 10:34.800
I'm sorry for dragging you into this...

10:34.880 --> 10:39.050
I chose this of my own accord. It isn't your fault.

10:40.930 --> 10:45.970
Your mother was a famous dancer, right?

10:49.190 --> 10:54.270
Matching Yuki Ogata, the dancer, was my goal...

10:55.730 --> 10:59.150
I felt that that was everything to me.

10:59.240 --> 11:02.570
So after I was injured and quit ballet,

11:02.660 --> 11:08.250
I felt like I could never reach
that goal, that I had lost everything...

11:10.170 --> 11:14.670
Somewhere deep down, I felt a little relieved

11:14.750 --> 11:18.010
that I didn't need to
chase after my mother anymore...

11:18.090 --> 11:21.720
That I could go back to just being a fan...

11:23.010 --> 11:26.850
I had given up, but when I met
the Fuego it felt like I could dance again

11:26.930 --> 11:29.520
and I became ridiculously engrossed with it...

11:29.600 --> 11:31.310
Ogata...

11:31.390 --> 11:36.020
I was happy that I got to
meet you all and become friends.

11:36.110 --> 11:37.400
But...

11:39.400 --> 11:42.150
It's my fault.

11:42.240 --> 11:47.370
Why do the things I want
always turn out badly like this?

11:47.450 --> 11:52.080
Just when it feels like I've
gained something, I lose it right after...

11:56.920 --> 12:02.090
I don't care how dull and boring
and painful every day would be...

12:02.180 --> 12:04.930
I just don't want to lose anything else...!

12:50.520 --> 12:54.640
I know I'm in no position
to say so, but get out safely.

12:54.730 --> 12:56.480
You can count on me.

12:56.560 --> 12:57.600
Ogata.

12:59.650 --> 13:01.230
I'm sorry.

13:21.630 --> 13:23.420
There they go.

13:37.560 --> 13:40.940
I wonder what Suzuri said...

13:41.020 --> 13:43.780
She tried to tell me
something when she was on the Balon,

13:44.780 --> 13:49.870
but I couldn't hear her
over the sound of the monorail...

13:52.120 --> 13:55.160
I wonder what she said...

13:57.290 --> 14:00.920
She said she wanted to see you dance again.

14:01.000 --> 14:05.420
I wasn't going to
say anything, but Hishida told me

14:05.510 --> 14:08.590
that Suzuri mentioned it during the protest.

14:08.680 --> 14:15.270
She was just too worried that
saying it to you would've hurt you.

14:23.940 --> 14:25.730
Suzuri...

14:36.620 --> 14:38.790
This is H5.
Company-sized group of armed RideBacks

14:38.870 --> 14:41.670
spotted on the coastal
highway northwest of the base.

14:41.750 --> 14:44.590
It's the BMA! Confirming that
the black unit belongs to the leader!

14:44.670 --> 14:47.210
--What shall we do?
--Let them proceed.

14:47.300 --> 14:49.680
We'll play with them at the front gate.

15:11.320 --> 15:12.780
What was that...?!

15:55.490 --> 15:58.410
Your helicopter better show up.

15:58.490 --> 16:01.040
Don't worry. It's already here.

16:07.380 --> 16:08.840
<i>This is a RideBack.</i>

16:08.920 --> 16:11.720
<i>But why do you wanna know about RideBacks?</i>

16:11.800 --> 16:13.130
<i>That newbie's good!</i>

16:13.220 --> 16:15.140
<i>Face me in a RideBack race!</i>

16:15.220 --> 16:17.930
<i>"Fuego." It's Spanish for "fire."</i>

16:18.010 --> 16:19.140
<i>I'll protect you.</i>

16:19.220 --> 16:19.970
<i>Do you regret it?</i>

16:20.020 --> 16:23.770
<i>I'm just happy you've found</i>
<i>something to be engrossed in.</i>

16:23.850 --> 16:27.900
<i>I want to see you dance again, Rin!</i>

16:28.940 --> 16:31.030
Are you feeling nervous, Rin?

16:31.110 --> 16:32.320
Yeah...

16:32.400 --> 16:36.410
Just focus on dancing how your heart tells you to.

16:36.490 --> 16:38.530
The stage will answer back.

16:56.260 --> 16:57.430
Let's go.

17:08.110 --> 17:09.440
What are you doing?!

17:09.520 --> 17:12.110
I'm sorry! I can't go after all!

17:13.700 --> 17:16.070
Hold on! I'll bring her back!

17:21.080 --> 17:24.290
What is she doing?! There's no time!

17:24.370 --> 17:25.410
What's that...?!

17:44.020 --> 17:48.060
This is Unit 2.
Helicopter destroyed on rooftop in District 18 West.

17:48.150 --> 17:50.650
Now commencing infiltration of building.

17:53.480 --> 17:54.860
What was that?!

18:44.450 --> 18:46.240
What in the hell...?!

18:49.920 --> 18:51.290
Ogata!

18:56.090 --> 18:57.210
Where are you?

19:26.040 --> 19:27.490
Tamayo!

19:33.630 --> 19:36.800
RideBack squad is 2000 meters from base gate!

19:40.220 --> 19:42.720
--What's happened?!
--We have a system error!

19:42.800 --> 19:44.890
It might be an internal hack!

19:46.390 --> 19:48.430
Switching to backup system!

19:51.020 --> 19:53.100
LRS radar is picking up something!

19:53.190 --> 19:57.020
Missiles! They're below anti-aircraft artillery range!

19:57.110 --> 19:59.610
They knocked out our system?!

20:01.070 --> 20:02.280
The Goblin?!

20:37.020 --> 20:38.400
What the hell is...?!

21:05.720 --> 21:08.140
They've really done it this time.

21:08.220 --> 21:10.260
--Guttorm. Go and greet them.

21:10.260 --> 21:11.560
--Zero-one!
--Guttorm. Go and greet them.

21:11.640 --> 21:16.100
Grimoire floor sweep is complete.
Only a few hostiles remain.

21:16.190 --> 21:17.650
Now entering building.

21:41.170 --> 21:44.340
Two terrorists have fled
the building aboard RideBacks!

21:49.350 --> 21:50.390
Here they come...

21:56.730 --> 22:01.400
Even when he laughs

22:03.400 --> 22:08.990
I'm thinking of you before I realize it

22:12.030 --> 22:17.040
And the hands holding his

22:18.830 --> 22:24.300
feel your warmth, too

22:26.470 --> 22:30.220
Even if I cut out my recollections

22:30.300 --> 22:34.180
and drive them out of my heart

22:34.270 --> 22:37.930
or try to kick the memories out

22:38.020 --> 22:42.400
I still think of you

22:42.480 --> 22:46.900
Time now passes and seasons fly by

22:46.990 --> 22:50.740
Even if that smile starts to become hazy

22:50.820 --> 22:54.740
my heart will never forget you

22:54.830 --> 22:58.500
(even if we can never meet again)

22:58.580 --> 23:02.330
Even if I knock over photos of us smiling

23:02.420 --> 23:06.760
or try to hide my overflowing feelings

23:07.720 --> 23:10.970
my heart will never forget

23:11.680 --> 23:14.930
my memories with you

23:26.730 --> 23:32.160
Amid the dazzling colors of
the tearing wind and wavering flames

23:32.240 --> 23:34.410
the crimson iron horse gallops forward.

23:35.280 --> 23:39.790
On the final episode: "To the Stage of Light"
